  "body": "Stacked on #1935. The base branch is `issue/1927-contour-outside-hole-refusal`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Side Auto of a 2D Contour on picked rings now reads the part section at the rings' own level. It does not read the full XY silhouette. The floor of a blind bore filled that silhouette, so Auto resolved Outside on the bore rim and the #1927 law refused the pass.\n- New law `machining2d::auto_side` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_auto.rs`):\n  - It reads the section 0.01 mm under the top of the picks' Z span, then 0.01 mm over its bottom.\n  - At each probe it compares the area inside the rings with a 0.5 mm band outside the rings. A side holds material at a fill of 0.5 or more.\n  - Material inside only gives Outside. Material outside only gives Inside. The first probe that decides is the result.\n  - If the two probes decide differently, or if they see material on both sides and do not decide, the generate is refused by name: \"Side Auto cannot tell which side of the picked ring holds the material at Z ...: ... - set Side to Inside or Outside\".\n  - If no probe sees material on either side (a sheet part, a ring over the part in air), the part's XY outline decides, as before.\n- New `crates/app/src/operation/contour_auto_pick.rs`: it reads the Z span of the picks (in the setup frame, or along a tilted frame's axis) and the material, and calls the law.\n- `selection.rs` uses the new verdict in place of the old fill block. `generate.rs` refuses an Undecided verdict by name. `contour_auto_side` (the UI preview) maps Undecided to \"no answer\".\n- The rule applies only to `OpParams::Contour` with Side Auto. Plasma and wire contours do not use this verdict.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1933-contour-auto-side-level.md`.\n\n## Readings (tool centre to the wall, Ø6 tool, Side Auto, model top to model bottom)\n\n| Case | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Blind bore rim, Ø20 bore to floor Z 4, rim at Z 10 | Outside, refused \"set Side to Inside\" | Inside, centre 3.000 mm inside the wall (max error 0.000001), deepest level Z 4.000 (the floor), 0 gouges |\n| Same bore, floor rim at Z 4 | Outside | Inside, same pass, deepest level Z 4.000, 0 gouges |\n| Through hole Ø20 | Inside | Inside, centre 3.000 mm inside the wall, cut to Z 0, 0 gouges |\n| Boss 20 x 20 on a floor at Z 5 | Outside | Outside, centre 3.000 mm outside the wall, cut to Z 5, 0 gouges |\n| Block 40 x 40 outer wall | Outside | Outside, centre 3.000 mm outside the wall, cut to Z 0, 0 gouges |\n| `Milling-test.step` bore rim r 12.5 at Z 20 (Ø10 tool) | Outside, refused | Inside, the same moves as Side Inside, centre 5.000 mm inside the rim, 0 warnings |\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/contour_auto_level.rs` (new, 3 tests): `auto_on_a_blind_bore_rim_cuts_the_wall_from_inside_to_the_floor`, `auto_on_a_through_hole_rim_cuts_inside`, `auto_on_a_boss_and_on_an_outer_wall_cuts_outside`.\n- `crates/motion/tests/contour_auto_side.rs` (new, 6 tests): the law on boxes, the floor rim, the mid-solid refusal, the disagreeing probes refusal, the outline fallback and the empty part.\n- `crates/app/tests/area_open.rs`: `a_containment_that_puts_the_tool_in_the_part_is_refused_by_name`. Its last assert now expects the clean Inside pass in place of the refusal.\n- The #1935 refusals are unchanged: `contour_outside_hole` 5 of 5 pass.\n- `operations.rs` 120 pass, 6 ignored. This includes the sheet-part tests `contour_boss_pick_defaults_outside`, `a_closed_chain_routes_the_boundary_path_not_a_centerline` and `selection_notes_report_stitching_and_extension`.\n\n## Gate\n\nQuick gate on 13a1f2625 (`cargo xtask gate quick`, 36.6 min): post ok (11 s), motion ok (790 s), ui ok (58 s), app FAIL (1328 s) in 2 tests only: `setup_align::unverified_kinds_are_refused_while_verified_picks_generate_aligned` and `stitch_cross::a_self_touching_single_body_still_stops_at_its_top_level`. These 2 tests fail with the same message on the base #1935 head 0761173e8, without this change. They are not caused by this PR. New tests: `contour_auto_side` (motion, 6 pass), `contour_auto_level` (app, 3 pass).\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nTwo app tests fail on the base branch #1935 (head `0761173e8`) before this change, with the same message. I ran them on the base code to make sure:\n- `setup_align::unverified_kinds_are_refused_while_verified_picks_generate_aligned`\n- `stitch_cross::a_self_touching_single_body_still_stops_at_its_top_level`\n\nBoth fail with the #1927 refusal \"meets its wall at no level below the part top\". The first has Side Auto, and the Auto verdict there is Outside before and after this change. The second has Side Outside. These failures belong to #1935, not to this PR.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Side Auto under a tilted frame (the code reads the frame's local facets; no test).\n- Picks at several levels in one op: they share one verdict over their combined span.\n- Plasma and wire contours: the verdict is not used there. They lose the note \"machining inside the ring - the selection bounds air\", which they did not act on.\n- The GUI was not started.\n\nChangelog: 2D Contour Side Auto on a picked ring now reads the material at the ring's own level: a blind bore rim is cut from inside, and a ring that Auto cannot read is refused by name.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1933\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
